<title>USA: Paxson Communications buys Michigan station.</title>
<headline>Paxson Communications buys Michigan station.</headline>
<dateline>WEST PALM BEACH, Fla 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paxson Communications Corp said on Thursday it had acquired television station WJUE TV-43 from William B. Popjes for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Paxson said it now has a 100 percent ownership interest in the station, which serves Grand Rapids, Battle Creek, Kalamazoo and Lansing, Mich.</p>
<p>The station will now air Paxson's proprietary network of infomercials, inTV, and other mainstream programming, the media company said.</p>
